# Reviewed vulnerability baseline for the container images built in CI.
#
# The image scan gate blocks HIGH and CRITICAL findings. The list is empty on
# purpose: it was emptied when the base images moved to supported channels
# (mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0-noble, nginx:1.30-alpine-slim), and both
# now scan clean for fixable HIGH/CRITICAL findings.
#
# Rules for editing this file:
#   * only list findings that have a fix available (CI scans with
#     --ignore-unfixed, so unfixed findings never block);
#   * every entry needs a review note in the pull request that adds it, and the
#     list is re-reviewed at least quarterly and whenever a base image is bumped;
#   * never add an entry for a package the application itself pulls in - fix or
#     upgrade it instead;
#   * an empty list is the goal: prefer bumping the base image over adding a
#     line (see docs/guide/operations/security-checklist.md).
#
# Regenerate the candidate list with:
#   trivy image --scanners vuln --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed \
#     --format json -o /tmp/scan.json <image>
